Z||000000||fierospeeder||11-09-1999||03:14 PM||||I was wondering about getting a scantool, the kind that you can get real time info from the engine like digital volt readings, engine temp, fuel injection, mph, rpm, tps, etc...  I seen one from pepboys made by Sunpro, i have their fuel pressure and timing light, but they got a ScanTool, thats the name and im not sure of the cost.  I also seen one that Eastwood sells and also JC whitney that little hand held one.  Shade tree mechanic used some laptop with a special program and a link to do it.  I was wondering which is a good scan tool like one of those or the laptop one, and if anyone has suggestions.  I would like to get a laptop because used ones only cause 300 bucks.  If theres any scantools under 300 is what im looking for.  Thanks<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||11-09-1999||07:25 PM||||the AutoXray GM only scanner runs from around 150-190$us. Eastwood has them on the high end. (they are listed with the XP240 look down the list farther.) Unlike the XP240 these units are specific to GM and come with the cable. The XP240 requires additional cables at about 30$ each. Other people have these units for less than eastwood. I got mine for about 150$us.<P>Unless you need multi vehicle support there isn't much that competes with the GM only unit. All the Sun and Actron scanners I've seen require additonal parts/cables in addition to the scanner. these units will all run you around 300$us to start. More if you add aditional cars.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mwbackus||11-09-1999||07:33 PM||||The AutoXray GM scanner is availble from Summit :<BR>AXY-10110  $175.69 + $6.95 shipping<P>Checker Auto also has these, although you may have to order one in since it is rare to find one on their shelves.  Their price is only $149.99 so check with them first.<P>Oliver Scholz has designed a circuit for an ALDL to RS-232 PC interface:<BR> <A HREF="http://business.fortunecity.com/takeover/175/sc.html" TARGET=_blank>http://business.fortunecity.com/takeover/175/sc.html</A> <P> Although it seems cheap enough to make, the circuit does require a chip with a specialized ScanConverter software system embeded on it. Recent coorespondence indicated that he will supply this chip for $25 incl. shipping via airmail.<P>Mike||||reg||1
